  "interpretation": [
    "One million files includes 999,996 4 KiB files and four large/partial-range controls. Three new duplicate files are added during the experiment.",
    "Initial index and apply are single samples; idle and normal small-change cases have three samples each.",
    "Catch-up series include a metadata reconciliation pass and an already-idle confirmation pass. Inspect individual rows, not their combined median.",
    "Post-apply first pass refreshes mappings for 999,870 changed destinations without content reads. This cost is additional to initial apply.",
    "Each 4 KiB write in the shared 8 MiB destination hashes one 128 KiB logical chunk and reuses the other 63.",
    "The representative write invalidates 7,812 source-dependent completion records and replays 7,811 remaining duplicate targets, without rehashing those targets.",
    "Peak RSS measures the actual dedupit child via GNU time and excludes OS page cache and the driver.",
    "Times include guest filesystem synchronization, CLI startup and database commits. VM resources, storage and kernel differ from the previous host portable benchmark.",
    "All original bytes and inode identities and all new-file bytes were checked; complete native and fresh portable range inventories matched, with database integrity and foreign-key checks."
  ]
